sions, and an explicit statement that this documentary review grants no implementation or operational authority. Do not claim to recompute hashes, inspect omitted files, or validate runtime behavior. Do not call tools, modify artifacts, submit a follow-up, or authorize implementation/build/runtime/IPC/VM/D2/D3/commit/push.","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_0b401687b872f549016ace41700f008191a7f8d538eded0dc5","summary":[],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqzkFw_uDgsyTM5_YF7U0gVZ6U2xJPZqFSJtLgTRHI26TjercZHLqjw6Xz5TKsAWcLVUbttTrL6udlpUn5AqaBEMq-nU5Szh2v6gGInBLki_Q1P_uzzdVNFTj3SDj3Xx2SxJqZSRfalU5WfEyfaTrbz2KwKbbxWS_IAuHYIojV0mRn5kOw_08MvQBotHYl5To-qETLeab8KD7EVr7CqhnijUcPxMoiszdRyXSPRKizAO0jJnFUDnljAgWhl5USTzRWPzl6G_XJrB9zh16SYU-HBhPDdqTiZYHhed9XrJYxDYAtgWl5HjmTxiVWwKp0YCM_VHvRSZJSMxOTorEcdhjsS2mG07hfPseZt2TH0iM3lUtPLkycDcw5UKIQ3pEOmpS0ByIsRRZQ9VOV8AH8cSY-2tePnDyUfwA-bsVngMA6x6pPn-n1sQ1-3Y_Ur1OTRvAVintVANkD-KVUmIKtbmD22Lgs-x2m5zPKV9rkoTOhEYbEf6r7gjqk4VYWYXOKEUiKwerhpRnn0OtbT57wD6f_gsfAnrhHOcdcXSmxXMxwcVqS730O15mra_Fv9fGzUq_i6SATFs30NSglMdMDm2ShEB_jEf0xFZmAe9SB24ztMhwnFijzIVziHdPL8KwDy6fNqERcMWPpJQSN5Ex7ZG1U1Cx-WnoKcNOEOXNctwc6ShLNjTOulGVp61vTTXZcYg4eb49RIfnabSsYi9C7lUmA2qRWCwPYjncgSjpJnjUPkzZ14zTe376rtroJyXobmNCaHY7do09xzOmM0z4sGfebF7R5zBdUZIaEQjvVbSn3ckSSu9uf1TdT0zNgym5pdPinvFUi76uI5lDbcOiNQNs6OzHmebHl9DA7m5K50XX-KmXCmRBUoi2E4UYeK1B8sjsF9jZ-pYqhc6P5SxomyCtBcp-pK5-m3g934IOQXuoKV-dNSpov_S7c7fHrMzalFqBrsoBLoEKUVQWamJpiOAZE19RsqBTgJxJFUoib-AG8ifxNqPZB3_dloQjwN1k5W-LG24Uac8wbsOlscOxfvIg3San7hyE4VFx_WVskNVm0XUzk9h1oAF2MpiWF4uxkuz2OZfGh7pQIwo8Zn_f1VxrYAzMy0ZOmM5aCMWG-ar2HMIvQmiUkLFLUJwgUnScGjT3xl08lntNGVH3ZTdssNcD2OfcNCBUACj1Mtw9Qk-vNG01agVhPHHhm7H_SbPaT-_WWP1knavlc5Lv1WURBwz5cPqdAd-5xyEOiIB7X1YYEwgjvypfGejxsWmzW16BthZD2IrjTij369N_fjhSoIZncYJ78R1qupc0T4dzMLXuay4lR29Yhv_g7CawpD8pb-kTahtHkJGX-bPJwW_jSjiS1mScK0tHFvq3k-EMsEwnUyvlFz53M5KLhKLVd90U4JMFD9P6bNNr_XhTF-J6AT6_xZcUPoDyNp0xHPQtELekwAdJu7cjQYMuUYSJSaCt7ovM-vEzCz3XokIt2415Ga3SGs-hZPoUFYOYzV0XkmOH7U5Azf1jiUH97uOsZPTJoPlqJ66yr01qPQpEH_ESseMQ_TEnyZ8k2A23TaB8wZFSVc_1JLPc7B6TiHvg_7v3swS4BLmw_zOz2zxqeT0FgRsW_EEnKLKYC6E0dMzbsfnKKg_e_6Ys5iZZiLwQAqCH9qzmE1dXybFfUk6BYDH1JouWmr7FbK00-5KtrY7Q4Cv83z3pWgoBiYms71b5_8PR2wNGDrzBWhcsrcQAjmV2HEYb2APMjrzNe-R9Q0m8mAAybzLlguOGomP5rULtG7GQ7gVL5Lwj7Rvu_cBWP88-KUY9zaJGhdWDbwCqxEq2eO9LZarb_AN0rMG_Co1cU4IRLi3Jbat-YS4z1yeYHGCoQQBBzfYCHvajp1jm2CLRmayUyciSM8bjOhLQmG29Kz2AXk9_kg_RDnA7q3M05Rcv-tusWaSoECHGWrJmZayEjDAEbrkJaorlGpjC8Gc-C1Mn_OFMc0U28n5FteoJ-JM3qKk3f1OogiFxsn0N4_wLxCI11lBimzOBPRZ5e6GRk2SKiMK8Dj9jwv_8u6Zql8HepXl928xH5PsZVMOolm7eVeWzq0E0j3Cw6bfHcGJLVdJ4f8Vi11p7v7FllHqYz8LM-ZOknDU8-k6pVQenHuBQvFEdQCHi0vKs8FkAvxEGW5Puh46bms_oky3KTV4O_q1rn5VMAUeSgIgXp8PWYhGsqoclURz8bwkZQRdM21wFMQyWv8Y6QA71gDazicW4iD4pH64OCktakcSD_8v5CGP7iaNNhcDMIb6g="},{"type":"message","id":"msg_0b401687b872f549016ace417046548191a4e079a916d88e5e","role":"assistant","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"## Verdict: APPROVE\n\n**v1.16/r14 resolves the bounded r13 journal-policy contradiction and preserves the accepted r12 B1/B2 corrections at the documentary level.** This conclusion covers the supplied excerpts and active projections, not whole-file or runtime correctness.\n\n### Findings\n\n1. **The journal exception is explicit and narrowly scoped.**  \n   SPEC §7.1, numbered item 5, and §7.2 `AUTH-005` permit bounded, read-only parsing/replay of `reservation-journal.jsonl` solely to derive cleanup history under `COUT-001`–`COUT-004`. The previously conflicting manifest projections now expressly include that exception:\n   - `/sandbox/finalizer_ipc_boundary/abnormal_evidence_only/forbidden/3`\n   - `/semantic_finalizer_contract/finalizer_ipc_boundary/abnormal_evidence_only/forbidden/3`\n   - `/sandbox/inventory_requirements_by_mode/abnormal_evidence_only`\n   - `/sandbox/runtime_finalizer_cleanup`\n   - `/semantic_finalizer_contract/abnormal_evidence_only/non_control_validation`\n\n   The attached classification, mode-selection, artifact-check and failure-summary projections also reflect this distinction.\n\n2. **Unusable journal history does not become a final-record gate.**  \n   Invalid, unavailable, malformed, truncated or incomplete history yields `unknown` without blocking an otherwise authorised abnormal `INCONCLUSIVE` record. This is explicit in §7.1 item 5 and §7.2’s journal-history policy, including:\n   - `/classification_rules/abnormal_journal_history_policy`\n   - `/semantic_finalizer_contract/abnormal_evidence_only/journal_history_policy`\n\n3. **Other non-control evidence remains raw-only.**  \n   The attached abnormal-mode policies preserve/hash safely readable, bounded raw bytes without schema replay or normal bundle/inventory gates. Missing and unavailable evidence remain distinct; preserved post/final files do not establish verified or empty inventories.\n\n4. **Safety and authority restrictions remain intact.**  \n   Journal mutation, live IPC inspection, cleanup, retry and abnormal PASS/FAIL remain forbidden. Common authority failures block finalisation rather than authorising abnormal-mode entry. Historical cleanup completion never implies PASS.\n\n5. **The r12 corrections are preserved.**\n   - **B1:** §7.2 `JRN-002`–`JRN-009` retain distinct creation/cleanup pending states, orphan-outcome rejection, phase constraints and stable resource-identity continuity.\n   - **B2:** §7.1’s normal-finalisation paragraph and item 5, §7.2 `FIN-001`, and the attached failure-rule projections retain historical `complete` after later evidence/finalisation failure while overall status remains `INCONCLUSIVE`.\n\n### Must-fix blockers\n\nNone identified within this bounded amendment review.\n\n### Optional advice\n\nFor editorial clarity, qualify the generic inventory-parsing language at `/semantic_finalizer_contract/failure_summary_checks/3` explicitly by mode. The supplied abnormal-mode overrides already prohibit inventory replay and require unavailable post/final summaries, so this is not a blocker.\n\n### Context sufficiency and omissions\n\nThe supplied context is sufficient for this single contradiction-closure assessment. Omitted SPEC text and digest-only manifest sections—including `/evidence_recovery` and `/runtime_bundle`—were not inspected. Their hashes do not establish consistency.\n\nThe reported synthetic tests were not independently reproduced. The post-freeze checker/schema-validation sidecar is not supplied; full-interpreter, cross-artifact PID and production-finaliser behaviour remain unverified.\n\nThe packet identity is supplied as SHA-256 `c5d42e42ea1fcb015b393de59819fa7c89669cc9e56ba44a13e9c816b3c17e95`; I did not recompute it or other hashes, use tools, or inspect a filesystem.\n\n**This documentary review grants no implementation or operational authority. It does not authorise implementation, build, runtime, IPC/VM, D2/D3, commit, push or any follow-up submission/call, and does not establish or replace owner consent.**","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"6ce3194e-3c0d-4956-8c6d-b4e1398d2f6f","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"medium"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"medium","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":43208,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":907,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":50},"total_tokens":44115,"attribution":{"items":{"msg_0b401687b872f549016ace416a6144819185af09ffa0ac6ba8":{"input_tokens":42765,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"content":[{"input_tokens":42765,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}]},"msg_0b401687b872f549016ace417046548191a4e079a916d88e5e":{"input_tokens":0,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":857,"content":[{"input_tokens":0